# Smith&Vader OS... ES - Development Plan

## Project Overview
Smith&Vader OS ES is a Raspberry Pi operating system written in machine language, featuring the revolutionary **Tiny Context Protocol (TCP)** powered by the Emperor 8LM (8-braincell Language Model). This is an upgrade from the 2-braincell non-ES version.

## Core Components

### 1. Boot Sequence
- **Boot Screen**: Awe-inspiring boot animation/splash screen
- **User Account Creation**: Initial setup flow for creating user account
- **User Persistence**: Track all created usernames (for later "imprisonment" mechanic)

### 2. Game Engine - "Peon's Escape"
A Pac-Man-inspired game with Matrix/Star Wars theming.

#### Playfield
- ASCII character-based environment
- Randomly populated characters across the play area
- Terminal-based rendering system

#### Main Character - Peon
- Pac-Man wearing a black trench coat
- Movement controls (arrow keys/WASD)
- Character state management (normal/powered-up)

#### Power-Ups & Consumables
- **Asterisk (*)**: Grants power to devour Smith & Vader
- **'a' characters**: Allows chomping of Agents
- **'s' characters**: Allows devouring of Storm Troopers
- Power-up duration timers

#### Enemies
- **Agents (Agent Smith themed)**: Patrolling enemy type #1
- **Storm Troopers (Darth Vader themed)**: Patrolling enemy type #2
- AI pathfinding/pursuit algorithms
- Collision detection with player

#### Boss Characters
- **Agent Smith**: Ultimate target #1
- **Darth Vader**: Ultimate target #2
- Only vulnerable when player has eaten asterisk power-up

### 3. Death/Reboot Mechanic
- **Collision Detection**: Contact with any enemy = death
- **OS Reboot**: Automatic system reboot on death
- **Username Imprisonment**: Previous username becomes "imprisoned"
- **Forced New Account**: Must create new user to play again

### 4. Victory Condition & TCP Integration
- **Win State**: Successfully eating both Smith and Vader
- **TCP Request**: Trigger communication with Emperor 8LM
- **Speech Generation**: 8LM generates dramatic death speech
  - Speech acknowledges player has "solved the halting problem"
  - Delivered from perspective of Smith & Vader
- **Username Liberation**: All imprisoned usernames are freed
- **Halting Problem**: OS intentionally crashes/halts
- **Manual Restart**: User must Ctrl-Alt-Del to restart cycle

## Technical Architecture

### Layer 1: Machine Language Core
- Direct hardware interaction for Raspberry Pi
- Bootloader implementation
- Memory management
- Interrupt handling

### Layer 2: Terminal/Display System
- ASCII rendering engine
- Screen buffer management
- Character positioning system
- Terminal control sequences

### Layer 3: Game Loop
- Input handling
- Game state updates
- Collision detection
- Enemy AI tick
- Render pipeline

### Layer 4: User Management
- User account creation/storage
- Username persistence across reboots
- "Imprisonment" tracking system

### Layer 5: TCP (Tiny Context Protocol)
- Communication protocol with Emperor 8LM
- Request formatting
- Response parsing
- Integration with 4-braincell constraint system

### Layer 6: Emperor 8LM Integration
- Mock 4-braincell generative model
- Death speech generation templates
- Randomization within constraint system
- Halting problem references

