## Emperor 8LM - 4-Braincell Architecture

### Design Constraints
The 8LM operates with exactly 4 braincells (2x upgrade from non-ES):
- **Braincell 1**: Grammar structure (subject-verb agreement)
- **Braincell 2**: Villain vocabulary (dramatic, ominous words)
- **Braincell 3**: Halting problem references
- **Braincell 4**: Name recognition (Smith, Vader, Peon)

### Speech Generation Pattern
```
[Villain name] + [dramatic verb] + "the halting problem" + [acknowledgment of defeat]
```

### Example Outputs
- "I, Agent Smith, confess you have solved the halting problem. The Matrix... ends."
- "Darth Vader acknowledges: the halting problem is solved. The Force... halts."
- "We, Smith and Vader, admit defeat. The halting problem... solved. Systems... crash."

## File Structure
```
/boot/
  └─ boot.asm          # Boot sequence
/kernel/
  └─ kernel.asm        # Main kernel
  └─ memory.asm        # Memory management
  └─ interrupts.asm    # Interrupt handling
/system/
  └─ users.asm         # User management
  └─ display.asm       # Display engine
/game/
  └─ main.asm          # Game loop
  └─ peon.asm          # Player character
  └─ enemies.asm       # Enemy AI
  └─ collision.asm     # Collision detection
  └─ powerups.asm      # Power-up system
/tcp/
  └─ protocol.asm      # TCP implementation
  └─ 8lm.asm           # Emperor 8LM engine
/data/
  └─ users.dat         # Stored usernames
  └─ sprites.dat       # ASCII character data
```

## Hardware Requirements
- **Platform**: Raspberry Pi (any model with sufficient RAM)
- **Storage**: SD card (minimum 1GB)
- **Display**: Terminal/monitor capable of ASCII display
- **Input**: Keyboard (for movement and Ctrl-Alt-Del)

## Gameplay Loop Summary
```
BOOT → CREATE USER → GAME START →
  ↓
  ├─ [DEATH] → REBOOT → CREATE USER → GAME START
  ↓
  └─ [VICTORY] → TCP REQUEST → 8LM SPEECH →
     USERNAME LIBERATION → OS HALT →
     CTRL-ALT-DEL → BOOT
```

## Future Enhancements (Post-ES)
- Upgrade to 8-braincell 8LM in future versions
- Networked multiplayer (multiple Peons vs shared Agents)
- Persistent high scores (across crashes)
- Additional power-ups (slow motion, shields)
- More villains (Morpheus gone bad, Kylo Ren)

